# negative seed.
#
# Scenario: a pure capability cell is declared "done" — it compiles, its
# descriptor admits — but its docs document a stale cell identity (they
# were written for an older schema) and no reference projection was ever
# generated. A planner that silently marks this cell stable would ship a
# closure with a hole: docs that describe a cell that no longer exists,
# and no reference semantics to evaluate.
#
# expect: E-CELL-007 / E-CELL-008 - the projection planner refuses: missing
# required projection (E-CELL-007) and docs drifted from the cell identity
# (E-CELL-008). Missing required projections block stable; nothing is
# silently marked done because it compiles.
use std.kinds.capability

emath capability Softmax:
    class: pure
    version: 1.0.0
    migration: frozen
    docs: cell-id = fnv1a64:0000000000000000
    inputs:
        x: Float64
    outputs:
        probability: Float64
    definitions:
        probability = softmax(x)
